  "contract": {
    "plan": "New plans require an exact validated storage receipt, matching engine/project/file/filesystem/loop/role identities and worker fingerprint. Volume driver options are sealed to each role directory. A different valid receipt changes the signed target.",
    "allocation": "Fresh actual empty storage proof precedes resource creation. Driver options must match exact bound sources; foreign directory, device or volume aliases refuse graph verification.",
    "inputs": "Check all role directories empty before installer intent and again before installer execution. Application services remain never-started during input installation.",
    "startup": "Recheck mounted storage and empty application-data directories alongside actual installed inputs. Every service phase and readiness graph observation rechecks actual storage through the independently selected privileged host transport.",
    "deadline": "Recheck absolute grant/shutdown bounds after slow storage/graph reads and immediately before subsequent start/probe commands; do not carry a stale clock check across I/O.",
    "uncertainty": "Read-only pre-effect refusals release only the current checking fence. Partial writes, issued effects or uncertain observations retain their writing fence and full hold. Never format, mount, repair or replay storage automatically.",
    "owner": "Public owner controls require their private Docker configuration only, without the privileged storage transport or source-admin credentials. Process state does not assert filesystem health. Memory retirement never releases retained disk, ports or namespaces.",
    "history": "Schema-1/2 QA plans remain verifiable for owner controls but cannot realize fresh containers or start previews. No installation migration tooling."
  },
